From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle: battery empty at
 OnePlus' power-off voltage

bq27xxx writes the battery's voltage-min-design-microvolt to the bq27411
as its Terminate Voltage: the voltage at which the gauge's compensated
remaining capacity, and so its reported level, reach 0. 3.4 V came with
this device tree and does not match what OnePlus does on this phone.

OnePlus' charger code for the OnePlus 8 (LineageOS
android_kernel_oneplus_sm8250, drivers/power/oplus/oplus_charger.c, with
qcom,vbatt_power_off = <3250> in arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/19821/
kona-mtp.dtsi) keeps the shown level at 1% while the battery is above
3.25 V, even when the gauge reports 0, and powers the phone off once it
stays below 3.25 V. The OnePlus 8 Pro (19811) has a different cell and is
not a reference here.

With a worn cell the 3.4 V point comes early under load. Measured on an
IN2013 (2026-10-22): a game drew 3.6-3.8 A, the battery sagged to 3.32 V
and the gauge went from 48% to 0% within 20 s, then counted up from 0 for
days (the level is smoothed and may not jump back). On 2026-10-27, at
4.18 V while charging, it read StateOfCharge 15% against
StateOfChargeUnfiltered 62% and NominalAvailable/FullAvailable 2650/3155
mAh; FullChargeCapacityUnfiltered was 1317 mAh, the charge the gauge
expected to deliver above 3.4 V.

Set the battery's empty point to 3.25 V, where OnePlus powers this phone
off. It is inside the gauge's range (2800-3700 mV, TI SLUUAS7B, Data
Memory subclass 82 offset 16) and only changes what the gauge reports:
charging and the cell's own protection do not read it, and no other node
uses this battery. The power-off itself is done in userspace (ARMDeck's
op8-lowbatt) at the same voltage.

[ARMDeck: compile-tested only as of 2026-10-27; not yet on hardware.]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
@@ -353,7 +353,12 @@
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
 		energy-full-design-microwatt-hours = <16370000>;
 		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <4270000>;
-		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
+		/*
+		 * Where OnePlus powers this phone off (vbatt_power_off in the
+		 * vendor DT). bq27xxx writes it to the gauge as its Terminate
+		 * Voltage, the voltage at which the gauge reports 0%.
+		 */
+		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3250000>;
 		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4435000>;
 	};
 };
